.Dd September 17, 2026
.Dt GOLDIN 1
.Os "macOS"
.Sh NAME
.Nm /usr/local/bin/goldin
.Nd Divide an HFS/HFS+ file with 2 forks into a data fork and AppleDouble encoded resource fork.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl \-version
.Op Fl h , Fl \-help
.Op Fl s , \-strip
.Op Fl v , \-verbose
.Ar FILE|DIRECTORY [FILE|DIRECTORY]...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Goldin does the same job as 
.Xr SplitForks 1
with some enhanced functionality. It converts Macintosh HFS or HFS Extended 
("HFS+") two-fork files into AppleDouble format with the data fork and the 
resource fork plus file system metadata in separate files. The original 
SplitForks only acted on one file, goldin can act on more than one file and 
can also be invoked with one or more directories ans will search each 
directory recursively for files to convert,
.Pp
.Nm
accepts these options and arguments:
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Fl \-version
Show tool version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Show usage summary and exit.
.It Fl s , Fl \-strip
Strip the resource fork from the original file.  The default is to leave the resource file in place after copying it to its AppleDouble metadata file.
.It Fl v , Fl \-verbose
.It Ar FILE|DIRECTORY ...
The file to split.  
.El
.Pp
.Sh FILE|DIRECTORY
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It example     - a file to convert
.It example.d/  - a directoru to search for files0 to convert
.El
.Sh NOTES
Goldin will fail with an error if the file(s) are not on an HFS/HFS+ volume
.Pp
Goldin lives here: https://github.com/packagesdev/goldin.
.Sh SEE ALSO 
.Xr SplitForks 1 , 
.Xr FixupResourceForks 1 , 
.Xr goldout 1 , 
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 1740 documents AppleSingle/AppleDouble formats.